      {
        "id": 59311,
        "name": "Objulen",
        "username": "Objulen",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/o/779978/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-11-13T05:37:32.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Tire Iron can be a great combo with&nbsp;<span>Alternating Tiger Claw against high DR opponents. I was playing against Apostate in the game, and, as usual, he was able to get out relics with incredibly high DR. Being able to knock them out when they hit 3 HP -- especially for the gauntlet and the tome -- was very handy. Low HP and high DR targets don't tend to be incredibly common, but like most of Mr. Fixer's abilities, it's situational: I threw out Jack Handle at one point and had Unity hit him with the card that lets someone use a power with +2 damage.</span></p><p>Riveting Crane is the style I tend to use the least, though it's vital many foes if you have Chrono-Ranger on your team to let him operate at complete functionality.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 80,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:35:04.574Z",
